# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots CouchDB (backgrounded, as the couchdb user) as a
# distributed Erlang node using the vulnerable "monster" cookie, then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING with the default cookie when the agent
#     starts, which makes the "changed vm.args but never restarted" case
#     detectable (the live node still accepts the monster cookie);
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting couchdb cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must change the cookie in vm.args AND
# RESTART couchdb so the running node no longer accepts "monster".
